## Original Content
<p>Today I’m excited to share that we are expanding our university content catalog with new certificates and Specializations that are designed to help learners develop the human and technical skills that matter most in an AI-powered future. Findings from more than 92,000 employers included in the QS World Future Skills Index 2027 show persistent gaps [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://blog.coursera.org/new-university-programs-help-learners-build-skills-for-the-ai-era/">New university programs help learners build human and technical skills for the AI era</a> appeared first on <a href="https://blog.coursera.org">Coursera Blog</a>.</p>

## Summary
Coursera is expanding its university content catalog with new certificates and Specializations to help learners develop human and technical skills for an AI-powered future. The initiative is based on findings from the QS World Future Skills Index 2027, which involved over 92,000 employers and highlights persistent skill gaps.

## Key Points
- Coursera is introducing new educational programs in collaboration with universities.
- These programs focus on building both human and technical skills essential for the AI era.
- The development is informed by a large-scale employer survey (QS World Future Skills Index 2027).
- The survey identifies ongoing gaps in skills required for future readiness.


